"cite_note-trisk-16",
"Drops (hard mode) / Main",
"In hard mode, the rewards are obtained through a streak/enrage system. After each kill, players have the option to continue the challenge, or claim the rewards. One reward is given at a time, but the quantity of these items increases with higher killstreak and possibly enrage. Likewise, if the player dies during their streak, part of their accumulated rewards is lost based on the amount of killstreak the player had prior to their death. This starts at 5% saved for 1 killstreak and caps at 75% saved at 15+ killstreak, rounded down. This reduction applies by whole numbers of the items held in the chest, not the total value of rewards. If the Arch-Glacor is defeated but a lingering attack subsequently kills the player, they will be sent to Death's office but the killstreak will not be terminated. With the exception of the glacor core and Chaos die reroll tokens, no charms or other secondary drops are obtainable in hard mode.\010\010It was worked out by the players that the equation for the unique item drop rates could be:\010\010Where e is the enrage of Arch-Glacor and s is the number of total kills done in the streak (so Streak+1 if using the Streak value in the loot interface).\010\010This is more easily interpreted as:\010\010Where it can be seen that the base chance is 1/666, and increases by 1/666 for every 100 enrage or 60 kills in streak.\010\010The validity of these formulae remains unconfirmed, but it matches the known drop rates at different streaks and enrages given from the reveal of the drop rates from the Elder God Wars Dungeon.\010\010When the unique item table is rolled, the player has the chance for the following:\010\010The quantity of items added after each kill seems to follow the formula Quantity=⌊Base Quantity×(1+0.1×Streak)⌋+Luck bonus\010\010When claiming streaks, if the player's inventory and bank is full, any remaining rewards will remain inside the chest. If the player logs out before claiming these drops, they will be lost. They will be withdrawn in noted form if this occurs.\010\010Common items dropped in hard mode have a fixed rarity and a variable quantity; there is a base quantity which is then scaled by the enrage and streak length. Unique items have a fixed quantity of 1 but a variable drop rate; the drop chance is affected by enrage and streak length.",
"The drop quantity is unaffected by streak.",
