"Giant mole",
"After fighting the mole, it is decided if a rare unique item will be dropped, and what that item is, before attributing it to a player. The odds of any rare item dropping at all are 1/10. After it is determined that a rare item will drop, which specific item is to be dropped is determined using a 52-slot table. This rare item is then distributed to one of the top three players, or to the single player if fighting the mole solo. All of the mole's special drops (clingy moles, numbing roots, dragon 2h swords, and ultra-growth potions) are tertiary drops. Whenever someone receives a special drop from the mole, it will be announced in the message box.\010\010The drop mechanics for the mole function differently in a group than when fought solo. Namely, the player to deal the most damage will always receive big bones and a mole claw if on a members' world, or only big bones if on a F2P world; the three players to deal the most damage will receive three mole skins, distributed equally (if the group is two players, there is a random chance for either player to receive two, and the other will receive one), all players who have completed the elite Falador achievement set will receive a mole nose, and players doing the Fur 'n Seek wishlist will sometimes receive long, sharp claws. The regular item drops are then divided equally between the top 3 players; if the drop quantity does not divide equally, the remainder is given to a random player of the top three that did not receive a rare drop.\010\010In hard mode, rare unique drops are more common, while some items are dropped in larger quantities.\010\010Following the 27 January 2014 update, the giant mole no longer has access to the rare drop table.",
"In a group, the big bones and mole claw are received by the player that dealt the most damage.",
"Mole claw (m)",
"Mole skin",
"In a group, the mole skins are distributed amongst the three players that dealt the most damage.",
"Mole nose (m)",
"Mole nose is only dropped with Falador shield 4 unlocked (does not have to be equipped).\010\010In a group, a mole nose is received by all eligible players that participated in the kill.",
