"Nex, Angel of Death",
"The Angel of Death has two tables; the first drop table is the main drop table, where unique items (wand, core, codex, and chest) can be rolled. The main drop table can be accessed by holding Nex's aggression the longest (capped at 1 player) or dealing the most damage (capped at 6 players) - therefore, each kill always has seven rolls on the main drop table, provided that seven players survived the encounter. All rolls are independent of each other, so it's possible to get multiple unique drops per kill, albeit very rare.\010\010A second, inferior drop table is awarded to the next top three damage dealers who are not eligible to roll for the main drop table. This is only accessible when fighting Nex in a group of eight or larger, and does not have access to the unique items.\010\010Regardless, both drop tables have access to the blood tentacle pet unlock item.\010\010The chance per person to obtain either the wand of the praesul or the imperium core is 1/(142×n) where n is the player count at the beginning of the fight; this is done such that the expected number of wands/cores come out to the same number per kill: 1/142 (given the player count is between 1 and 7). The per person drop rate to receive either a wand or core for team sizes of 8 or higher is 1/5000 for those who roll on the primary table. After the changes released on 7 May 2019, the praesul codex has a drop rate of 1/(36×min(7,n)) per person; this is done such that the expected number of codices come out to the same number per kill: 1/36 (after failing to receive either the wand or core). Therefore, the expected number of wand, core or codex drops per kill is approximately 1/29.\010\010Unlike the base Nex encounter, the Angel of Death does not have access to the rare drop table.",
"The Promised Gift",
"If the books are not received from killing Nex, the teleport shard at the end of a kill may be searched for them instead.",
"The Praesul",
"cite_note-book-5",
