"Torag the Corrupted",
"Torag does not drop his main rewards directly; instead, his equipment is added as possible rewards from the Barrows chest. See The Barrows Brothers#Rewards for more information. However, Torag can directly drop the following items.",
"Tormented demon",
"The main drop table is rolled out of 256. This is reduced to 253 if tier 3 or higher luck is active, which slightly reduces the chance of a fire talisman drop, and increases the chances of other main drops. Dragon platebody parts are rolled separately.",
"There is a 1/352 chance to access the dragon platebody part table (1/348 with tier 3 or higher luck active). If successful, one of the three parts is chosen (1/3 chance each).\010\010If a Most Wanted card (tormented demons) is carried, and if none of the uniques are selected (dragon platebody parts, dragon claws, dragon limbs), a second more generous roll is performed for each. For dragon platebody parts this is 1/334 (1/331 with tier 3 luck). Combining these chances gives an overall 1/515.9 chance to get each dragon platebody part per kill (1/509.9 with tier 3 luck). If the second roll results in a drop, additional charges are consumed from the card: 19 for dragon platebody parts.\010\010Receiving a dragon platebody part prevents all other drops except charms.",
"Ruined dragon armour slice",
"1/1,056; 1/1,044; 1/515.9; 1/509.9",
"1/352 chance for any ruined dragon armour piece. 1/1,044 (1/348 for any) with tier 3 luck or higher. Increased to 1/515.9 for a specific part while carrying a Most Wanted card (tormented demons), and 1/509.9 with a card and tier 3 luck active.",
"0.0947",
"Ruined dragon armour lump",
"Ruined dragon armour shard",
"cite_note-dragon-2",
"Dragon claws and limbs",
"Dragon claws (both are dropped as one drop) and dragon limbs each have a 1/256 chance to be dropped, as part of the main drop table (1/253 with tier 3 luck).\010\010If a Most Wanted card (tormented demons) is carried, and if none of the uniques are selected (dragon platebody parts, dragon claws, dragon limbs), a second more generous roll is performed for each. For dragon claws and limbs, this is 1/243 (1/240 with tier 3 luck), after the second roll for dragon platebody parts; if successful, one of the two items is selected (1/2 for claws, 1/2 limbs). Combining these chances gives an overall 1/168.6 chance to dragon claws or limbs per kill (1/166.6 with tier 3 luck). If the second roll results in a drop, additional charges are consumed from the card: 19 for dragon claws and 99 for dragon limbs.",
