"Yakamaru",
"When Yakamaru is killed, its helmet remains and acts as a reward coffer to collect the drops. Yakamaru has several drop tables that are rolled on to constitute the loot. The consumable table is always rolled, summoning charms are commonly received, and tertiary drops may be received. If the unique drops table rolls either a Mazcab ability codex or piece of achto equipment, the main drop will not be received. If the unique drops table rolls Teci, the main drop table will be rolled multiple times.\010\010Marks of War: 600\010\010Yakamaru can only drop one item from this table. If no armour piece or Mazcab ability codex is dropped, the player will receive teci.\010\010A player that owns all six pieces of achto legs and bodies may continue to receive achto armour as drops, but the drop order will no longer be enforced. For example, it is possible to receive a second Achto Teralith leggings, followed by a third Achto Teralith leggings.\010\010Otherwise, armour is gained from Yakamaru in the following order: legs then body.\010\010Progressing in the drop order requires collecting all three of the previous equipment slot's achto equipment, so in order to receive an Achto Primeval robe top, they would have to get all Achto Tempest, Primeval and Teralith legs. The Achto equipment gained from each equipment slot is based on the combat style the player dealt the most damage with during the kill they obtained that armour; if the equipment piece corresponding to the used style is not owned, that is always gotten before the others, and otherwise there are equal odds of obtaining armour corresponding to one of the unused styles.\010\010When killed in the wilderness with achto armour, it will drop a specified amount of coins if you die.",
"1,000–1,750",
"1/1.09",
"Achto Primeval robe top",
